The adaptive controller performed better than the fixed baseline in these five constructed scenarios. That’s an engineering demonstration, not evidence of real-world predictive accuracy.

One useful result: it didn’t simply apply more corrective resources. It generally used less total intervention while achieving lower modeled disruption, because it concentrated its actions and stopped when the simulated problem subsided.

