5. What we’ve actually added to Pantheon

We now have a practical demonstration of an adaptive coordination layer connecting independently modeled processes.

The next important work is replacing synthetic stress values with observations, expanding the model beyond tension and readiness, and testing its recommendations against independent human judgments.

But the architecture itself gives us an interesting new distinction:

A resilient system recovers from disturbance. A metaresilient system can also change how its constituent systems interact so that future disturbances propagate differently.

That’s the bigger NTE-of-NTEs opportunity: not merely managing individual trajectories, but learning which relationships between them make the whole more capable.

We have implemented the initial coordination mechanism and measured it within its simulated environment. The next threshold is proving that it works outside the environment we designed.